*
!.gitignore
!*.md

# Mutation-testing artifacts are REVIEW MATERIAL, not scratch (Codex round 11P's
# [medium] #4). A mutation matrix is evidence about the tests, and the reviewer being
# asked to trust it has to be able to read the applier that produced it and re-run the
# spec. So a `<wave>-mutations/` directory tracks its applier and its spec; its
# transcripts are markdown and `!*.md` above already covers them.
#
# Everything else here stays ignored, which is the point of the `*` at the top: the
# ~1.9MB of `review-*.diff` exports are derived from git history and belong nowhere
# near it.
!*-mutations/
!*-mutations/*.py
!*-mutations/*.json

# Same argument for measurement probes (R-001 and successors): an observed-throughput
# number is evidence only if the reviewer can read the probe that produced it and re-run
# the spec. A `<name>-probe/` directory tracks its script and its machine-readable results.
!*-probe/
!*-probe/*.py
!*-probe/*.json
!*-probe/*.go

# Persona consult archives are BINDING RULINGS the P3 design/plan cite as authority
# (Codex P3 plan-review round 2 [NEW-M]: the `*` above excluded the directory, and
# `!*.md` cannot re-include descendants of an excluded directory — the archives were
# silently untracked). Re-include the directory; `!*.md` then covers its files.
!p3-consults/
